    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen visually selecting, all atoms are deferred into a single Visual composite sequence. This makes it impossible to create an autocmd that runs on every individual atom in visual mode.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt would be possible to hook into individual visual atoms. Maybe a separate CmdAtomVisual autocmd?",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Do the subatoms in `CmdAtom.atoms` represent what you want? Except they arrive \"too late\"?\n\n> create an autocmd that runs on every individual atom in visual mode.\n\nThat also implies \"immediate\" (non-deferred) behavior. CmdAtom is intentionally deferred, i.e. it emits after an action, not during/before. ",
